 [0m[38;2;238;238;235m▪ [0mThis is [0m[1mHerdr Mobile Relay [0m— a Herdr plugin that lets you control Herdr agents from your phone.
 
   - [0m[1mWhat it does[0m: each Linux/macOS machine runs a relay; a phone connects directly (via Cloudflare tunnel) and merges all agents into one installable
   web app. You can start/stop/rename agents, send prompts, terminal keys, screenshots, and answer Codex/Claude Code/Qoder approvals, with push
   notifications.
   - [0m[1mStack[0m: Go backend ([0m[38;2;149;124;173mcmd/[0m, [0m[38;2;149;124;173minternal/[0m, [0m[38;2;149;124;173mrelay/[0m), Svelte frontend ([0m[38;2;149;124;173mfrontend/[0m), Makefile build, contracts and Playwright/unit tests.
   - [0m[1mSetup paths[0m: Quick Start (temporary TryCloudflare tunnel + QR) or stable install with your own Cloudflare domain and a user service.
   - [0m[1mCurrent version[0m: 0.13.5.
 
   There are uncommitted changes touching [0m[38;2;149;124;173mTerminalView.svelte[0m, [0m[38;2;149;124;173mterminal.ts[0m, tests, plus untracked review docs ([0m[38;2;149;124;173mCOPY_BUTTON_REVIEW*.md[0m, [0m[38;2;149;124;173mWATCHDOG.yml[0m) —
